Job Description
We’re looking for a junior videographer who is practical, technically capable, organised, and eager to grow. This is not a film industry role or a highly conceptual creative position.
We need someone who can produce clear, useful, well-shot content that supports marketing, product education, and customer engagement. The work should feel commercial, accessible, and grounded.
The Role
Run the content pipeline for marketing, product education and customer engagement: product demonstrations, how-to and troubleshooting videos, promotional edits, branch and event coverage, and platform-native short-form for Instagram, Facebook, TikTok, YouTube, WhatsApp and web.
What You'll Do At Adendorff
Plan, shoot and edit product-led video in-house and on location, often solo;
Own post-production: grading, audio, captions, motion graphics, multi-format exports;
Publish across platforms; keep the content calendar honest;
Read analytics and act: what worked, why, and what we make next;
Turn one shoot into a family of assets; set the quality bar for the brand.
What Good Looks Like (first 6 months)
The pipeline runs without chasing: briefs in, published assets out, on time, at a standard the brand can stand behind. Product demos that make a machine understandable to a tradesperson in under a minute. Measurable lift in reach and engagement, and they can tell you why it happened.
Essentials
2+ years producing video professionally, with a portfolio personally shot and edited;
Strong command of Premiere Pro or DaVinci Resolve, plus short-form fluency;
Competent solo shooter: camera, lighting and audio that make a warehouse look deliberate;
Motion graphics and caption competence (After Effects or equivalent);
Platform literacy: has published content and owned the numbers.
What Sets You Apart
In-house content for a physical-product brand; an audience grown with numbers you can defend; photography, drone or gimbal work; comfort filming in workshops, warehouses and events; genuine interest in tools and machines.
Why Adendorff
Impact: Your work is seen daily across South Africa;
Growth: Exposure to packaging, retail marketing, and AI-driven workflows;
Stability: A privately owned, South African-built retailer with a long-term mindset.
Closing Date
30 September 2026

