PURPOSE OF THE JOB:
To provide strategic leadership in the design and delivery of high-impact University events that advance institutional goals, foster stakeholder engagement, and strengthen the University's national and global reputation. This role ensures the alignment of event strategies with the University's vision, upholding protocols, governance, and brand standards while managing the full event lifecycle with professionalism, innovation, and precision.
The incumbent will be responsible to:
Lead the development and implementation of comprehensive project plans for the annual institutional events calendar;
Draft and submit detailed event briefs, creative concepts and communication strategies aligned with the University's marketing and brand objectives;
Manage the planning and execution of assigned University events, ensuring quality, consistency, and alignment with institutional priorities;
Oversee venue sourcing, setup, and supplier coordination in compliance with procurement protocols and brand identity;
Liaise with Security Services, protocol officers, and key stakeholders to finalise guest lists, scripts, signage, seating, dietary needs, and VIP arrangements;
Manage strategic faculty events hosted by the Vice-Chancellor, ensuring alignment with institutional goals and elevated visibility;
Provide project leadership and protocol guidance to faculty staff for event conceptualisation and execution;
Coordinate all aspects of event delivery, including venue, décor, catering, protocol, guest logistics, compliance and promotions;
Compile accurate event budgets and cost estimates in collaboration with the PR & Events Manager and/or Deputy Director;
Source competitive supplier quotations and ensure adherence to procurement and financial policies;
Track budget performance throughout the event lifecycle, implementing controls to prevent over-expenditure;
Conduct post-event debriefings and compile comprehensive closing reports within 14 days of event conclusion;
Develop and distribute event surveys to selected attendees to gather feedback and satisfaction indicators;
Analyse event outcomes, document lessons learned and develop best practice guidelines for future events.
MINIMUM REQUIREMENTS:
A relevant 3-year Bachelor’s degree in Event Management, Public Relations, Marketing, Hospitality Management, or a related field or;
5 years with a Project Management Diploma and/or Protocol Certificate, with clear evidence of application in large-scale event coordination;
Operational and strategic event planning, demonstrating responsibility for full project lifecycles from initial concept through to execution and evaluation;
High-profile event coordination, including logistics, stakeholder management, executive protocol and brand-aligned delivery within complex environments;
Application of protocol and ceremonial procedures, particularly in events involving executive leadership, government officials, or international delegates;
Client-facing consultation and brief interpretation, including the ability to translate strategic objectives into practical event outputs;
Budget development and financial management, with hands-on experience in vendor engagement, procurement processes, and expenditure tracking;
Team leadership and supervision, including the coordination of support staff, temporary teams and service providers for on-site delivery;
Experience in planning, coordinating, and delivering complex events in a high-profile environment (e.g., university, government, corporate), including protocol-sensitive events.
